    {
      "id": "claim_82fa67a81af44e189081612af123bf42",
      "statement": "Self-consistency voting derives confidence by running classification N times and computing the agreement rate (e.g., 5/5 identical→1.0, 3/5→0.6); the winning category is the modal label across runs, with ties or low counts resolving to the reserved 'unknown' category",
